	"department": "MUSIC",
	"description": [
		"Musical transmission between generations in the context of spiritual practice is a hallmark of music education in India. Students explore the challenges local educators face when bringing folk and ritual traditions into an urban folk school setting in Assam. Students experience connections between music and spirituality first-hand as they learn to perform songs and dances from culture bearers who introduce them to these participatory traditions in intergenerational environments. Open to students in all majors. Offered periodically during January term."
	],
